oxymesh — MeshCore-compatible firmware, written in Rust.

This project reimplements MeshCore's protocols (over-the-air packet format and companion
protocol) from a reading of its sources. No MeshCore file is copied.

  MeshCore — https://github.com/meshcore-dev/MeshCore
  Copyright (c) 2025 Scott Powell / rippleradios.com
  MIT License. Reference version: companion-v1.18.0 (commit 81dbae5, 2026-10-15).

Hardware facts about the ThinkNode M5 (pinout, battery curve) also come from Meshtastic's
ELECROW-ThinkNode-M5 variant (GPL-3.0, commit 9bcf0f7); no code is taken from it.
The SSD1681 display driver is written from the datasheet, without reusing GxEPD2 (GPL-3.0).

The firmware embeds a modified copy of trouble-host 0.7.0 (firmware/esp32s3/vendor/trouble-host):
  trouble — https://github.com/embassy-rs/trouble
  Copyright the Embassy project contributors. Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
  Change: set_passkey backported from trouble-host 0.8.0 (vendor/trouble-host-passkey.patch).

